ommunity Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9fa41fa57b22","stem":"What impact do plant-based diets have on urban air quality? - A) Negatively impact air quality - B) Have no effect - C) Improve air quality - D) Increase air pollution Answer: C) Improve air quality","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0f422235ccf2","stem":"Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of a plant-based diet? - A) Emphasis on whole foods - B) Exclusion of animal products - C) Focus on processed foods - D) High intake of fruits and vegetables Answer: C) Focus on processed foods","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7e371e21fd82","stem":"What is a key consideration for balancing a plant-based diet? - A) Avoiding all fats - B) Ensuring nutrient diversity - C) Limiting fiber intake - D) Increasing animal protein Answer: B) Ensuring nutrient diversity","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9f13b517d903","stem":"Which food group is central to plant-based diets for providing essential fats? - A) Nuts and seeds - B) Dairy - C) Meat - D) Sugary snacks Answer: A) Nuts and seeds","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cdd4c923a97f","stem":"How can plant-based diets support global health initiatives? - A) By increasing healthcare costs - B) By reducing the burden of chronic diseases - C) By decreasing public health awareness - D) By limiting nutritional access Answer: B) By reducing the burden of chronic diseases","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-425561cb664b","stem":"Which practice is NOT recommended for individuals on plant-based diets? - A) Monitoring nutrient intake - B) Eating a variety of plant-based foods - C) Skipping meals - D) Using supplements as needed Answer: C) Skipping meals","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a2fbc3991df5","stem":"What effect do plant-based diets have on land use according to the document? - A) Increase land use - B) Decrease land use - C) Have no effect - D) Cause land degradation Answer: B) Decrease land use","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8cc23ee7a26b","stem":"Which of the following is a recommended source of calcium in a plant-based diet? - A) Leafy green vegetables - B) Red meat - C) Fish - D) Dairy products Answer: A) Leafy green vegetables","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-33a4be93ab71","stem":"What is a common concern regarding the nutrient adequacy of plant-based diets? - A) Excessive fiber intake - B) Insufficient vitamin D - C) High cholesterol levels - D) Overconsumption of carbohydrates Answer: B) Insufficient vitamin D","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f9243db583a7","stem":"Which of the following environmental impacts is associated with a reduction in animal-based food consumption? - A) Increased greenhouse gas emissions - B) Decreased biodiversity - C) Improved land and water use efficiency - D) Increased water pollution Answer: C) Improved land and water use efficiency","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4e1e0fdae691","stem":"How do plant-based diets influence the overall carbon footprint? - A) Increase the carbon footprint - B) Have no effect on the carbon footprint - C) Reduce the carbon footprint - D) Exponentially increase the carbon footprint Answer: C) Reduce the carbon footprint","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-80ad07bc86b0","stem":"What type of plant-based diet includes small amounts of animal products? - A) Vegan - B) Flexitarian - C) Vegetarian - D) Pescatarian Answer: B) Flexitarian","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f0c2aec87105","stem":"Which aspect of plant-based diets contributes to their sustainability? - A) Reduced dependency on fossil fuels - B) Increased reliance on monocultures - C) Higher greenhouse gas emissions - D) Greater water consumption Answer: A) Reduced dependency on fossil fuels","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2e381d32ddcd","stem":"What is a recommended approach to increase the adoption of plant-based diets in communities? - A) Limiting plant-based food availability - B) Promoting education and accessibility - C) Reducing plant-based food variety - D) Ignoring dietary preferences Answer: B) Promoting education and accessibility These questions cover various aspects of plant-based diets as discussed in the WHO document, focusing on health, environmental impact, and sustainability.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Medicine","topic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d13f2a884eed","stem":"5. Recommendations24 REFERENCES25 APPENDICES27 Appendix 1: Data Collection Tool27 DODOSO KUHUSU UPUNGUFU WA DAMU KWA AKINA MAMA WAJAWAZITO / QUESTIONNAIRE ON ANEMIA IN PREGNANT WOMEN27 DECLARATION AND CERTIFICATION Declaration We (undersigned) declare that this research proposal is our own original work and it has not been submitted and will not be submitted to any other university for a similar or any other degree award and is not previously or currently under copyright. Name Signature Date","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["source_attribution_or_footer"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5217231c163a","stem":"2 Study Population The study population was all the pregnant women who were attending antenatal care clinic in Mawenzi Regional hospital","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-abe3218d840c","stem":"3 Inclusion and exclusion criteria. Inclusion Criteria Pregnant women aged 14 years or older attending antenatal care clinic at Mawenzi Regional Hospital, Willing to provide informed consent and who were able to communicate in Swahili or English. Exclusion Criteria Pregnant women with severe anemia (hemoglobin level less than 6 g/dL), pregnant women with known chronic medical conditions that could cause anemia, such as sickle cell disease or thalassemia. Reasons for Exclusion Severe anemia is a serious condition that requires immediate medical attention and is not suitable for participation in a research study. Pregnant women with known chronic medical conditions may have confounding factors that could affect the results of the study.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d7567f861f04","stem":"4 SAMPLe size The minimum sample size was calculated using the Cochran formula below: n = Z2P(1-P) £2 Where n = Sample size Z = Z-score which is set at 1.96 at 95% confidence interval P = Expected proportional previous prevalence 47% (Stephen et al., 2018) £ = Maximum likely error tolerance (10%) or 0.1 N = 1.962x 0.47(1- 0.47) = 96","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Epidemiological Measures","topicOriginal":"Epidemiological Measures","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Epidemiological Measures","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-25c2bc75a956","stem":"7 DATA processing and analysis Descriptive statistics were used to describe the sample population and the prevalence of anaemia. Data were analysed using Microsoft Excel, variables were summarised by frequencies and cross tabulation, which were presented with a bar chart and pie chart. Multivariate analyses were used to control for confounding factors and identify the independent predictors of anaemia.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3c96d02c55e7","stem":"1 Adverse Outcomes Anemia in pregnancy has been linked to adverse maternal and perinatal outcomes, including increased risk of maternal mortality, low birth weight, and preterm birth. Our findings support these associations, underscoring the critical need for effective anemia prevention and management strategies in pregnant women to improve both maternal and fetal health outcomes.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0165e5025355","stem":"2 Public Health Implications The high prevalence of anemia in our study population suggests a substantial public health challenge. The findings underscore the need for targeted interventions to address the identified risk factors. Strategies could include early ANC booking and provision of education on how to better improving dietary diversity, enhancing prenatal care services, and ensuring better access to iron and folic acid supplements.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-55388726d7a5","stem":"3 Study Limitations It is important to acknowledge the limitations of our study. The cross-sectional design limits the ability to establish causal relationships. Additionally, the exclusion of known anemia cases before pregnancy may have led to an underestimation of the true prevalence. Future research should aim to include longitudinal data to better understand the temporal relationships and causal pathways of anemia in pregnancy. Moreover, expanding the study to include a larger and more diverse sample could provide more generalizable findings.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-24d7b3b0ca33","stem":"5. Recommendations Policymakers should develop and implement comprehensive strategies to combat anemia in pregnancy. These strategies should include early ANC booking and provision of education on how to fortifying staple foods with iron and other essential micronutrients, providing free or subsidized iron and folic acid supplements, and training healthcare providers on the latest guidelines for managing anemia in pregnancy. Additionally, integrating anemia prevention programs into existing maternal and child health services can enhance their reach and impact. REFERENCES","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3efd373badc2","stem":"S. Ononge, O. Campbell, and F. Mirembe, “Haemoglobin status and predictors of anaemia among pregnant women in Mpigi, Uganda,” BMC Research Notes, vol. 7, no. 1, article no. 712, 2014. 13 L. H. Allen, “Anaemia and iron deficiency: effects on pregnancy outcome,” American Journal of Clinical Nutrition, vol. 71, no. 5, pp. 1280s–1284s, 2000.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5888c07c9228","stem":"Carroli, G., Rooney, C., & Villar, J. (2001). How effective is antenatal care in preventing maternal mortality and serious morbidity? An overview of the evidence. Paediatric and Perinatal Epidemiology, 15(s1), 1-42.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-41f1a292f351","stem":"Mbekenga, C. K., Pembe, A. B., Christensson, K., & Olsson, P. (2013). Pregnancy health education: What does it take to open the black box of routine antenatal care? A qualitative study in Tanzania. BMC Health Services Research, 13(1), 113. Okeke, E. N., & Ugwu, E. O. (2020). Impact of early antenatal booking on the prevalence of anemia in pregnancy in Enugu, Nigeria. APPENDICES Appendix 1: Data Collection Tool DODOSO KUHUSU UPUNGUFU WA DAMU KWA AKINA MAMA WAJAWAZITO / QUESTIONNAIRE ON ANEMIA IN PREGNANT WOMEN (Do not write names; all information will remain confidential) / (Usiandike jina; habari zote zitabaki kuwa siri) MAHALI / LOCATION: No. .................. HB .................. MKOA WA / REGION","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-f30ff07b7960","stem":"UPUNGUFU WA DAMU / ANEMIA: Je, ni mambo gani yanachangia upungufu wa damu kwa akinamama wajawazito? / What are the factors that contribute to anemia in pregnant women? (weka alama V/Check the appropriate box)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lishe duni / Poor diet"},{"label":"B","text":"Ugonjwa wa Malaria / Malaria"},{"label":"C","text":"Ugonjwa wa minyoo / Worms"},{"label":"D","text":"Uzazi wa mara kwa mara / Frequent childbearing"},{"label":"E","text":"Sijui / I don't know"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3c79cdc33ae5","stem":"DALILI ZA UPUNGUFU WA DAMU / SYMPTOMS OF ANEMIA: Je, unafahamu dalili za upungufu wa damu kwa akina mama wajawazito? / Are you aware of the symptoms of anemia in pregnant women? (Ndiyo/Yes / Hapana/No) Ikiwa ndiyo, taja dalili nne. / If yes, please list four symptoms.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"_____________________________________________________"},{"label":"B","text":"_____________________________________________________"},{"label":"C","text":"_____________________________________________________"},{"label":"D","text":"_____________________________________________________"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0e613bbe46d8","stem":"Health Facility Name: Social Information","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ed93f01bff15","stem":"2.2 Socio-Demographic Factors Several socio-demographic factors were identified as significant predictors of anemia in pregnancy. These include age, education level, and employment status. The highest prevalence of anemia was observed among participants with primary education (50%) and those who were self-employed (66.7%). These findings suggest that lower education levels and self-employment are associated with a higher risk of anemia, possibly due to limited access to health information and resources.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-527d69dda840","stem":"4.2 Prenatal Care Services Enhancing prenatal care services to include routine screening and timely management of anemia is crucial. Pregnant women should have regular hemoglobin checks and access to iron and folic acid supplements. Ensuring better access to these supplements can help mitigate anemia's effects.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cc36386d4726","stem":"5 Study Limitations The study has several limitations that need to be acknowledged. The cross-sectional design limits the ability to establish causal relationships between identified risk factors and anemia. Additionally, the exclusion of known anemia cases before pregnancy may have led to an underestimation of the true prevalence of anemia in the study population. Another limitation is the reliance on self-reported data for some variables, which may be subject to recall bias. Future research should include longitudinal data to better understand the temporal relationships and causal pathways of anemia in pregnancy. Moreover, expanding the study to include a larger and more diverse sample could provide more generalizable findings.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Public Health and Research","topic":"Obstetrics","topicOriginal":"Obstetrics","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Public Health and Research","displayTopic":"Obstetrics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8f978321e590","stem":"Cyclosporin causes the following","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Psychiatry","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Psychiatry","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"bf8550f965af061f34ae3c24186f33481f1aa7ee"},{"id":"q-65637ddb1c28","stem":"The following statements about the anti-inflamatory analgesics indicated are true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Psychiatry","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Asprin is valiable in the treatment of GI pain."},{"label":"B","text":"Paracetamol is a potent anti-inflamatory agent. T © Salicylates are effective in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis."},{"label":"D","text":"Indomethacin can displace warfarin on tolbutamide from plasma protein."},{"label":"E","text":"Aspirin has antipyretic activity."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Psychiatry","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFl