ent disease, and should be monitored without treatment until patients enter accelerated or blast phase."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Medicine","displayTopic":"Public Health and Community Medicine · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"a9cc316d7b49f30f77a979da5f9611174e594eb2"},{"id":"q-79c49fe52c50","stem":"Which of the following causes relaxation of Lower Esophageal Sphincter (LES).","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gastrin"},{"label":"B","text":"Proteins"},{"label":"C","text":"Chocolate"},{"label":"D","text":"Increased gastric distension"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4b4307a15a50","stem":"Which of the following is not true about Schatzki's ring.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"There is increased muscle fibrosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Hiatus hernia is invariably present"},{"label":"C","text":"Mostly it is asymptomatic"},{"label":"D","text":"It is present at the gastroesophgeal junction."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject"