 Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Neoplasia","topicOriginal":"Neoplasia","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Edema of the skin over the breast (peau d’orange)"},{"label":"B","text":"Carcinoma of the inflammatory type"},{"label":"C","text":"Edema of the arm"},{"label":"D","text":"An axillary node measuring 1.5 cm in diameter"},{"label":"E","text":"Satellite nodules in the skin over the breast"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Neoplasia","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0c9bf9da9abf","stem":"a 16 year old girl and her mother, who has had a radical mastectomy for carcinoma are extremely concerned about a 2cm irregular, firm, movable mass near the girl’s nipple. The mass has doubled in size during the two months since the first noticed it. Her breasts are otherwise normal. The most economical, acceptable next step is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Neoplasia","topicOriginal":"Neoplasia","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A needle biopsy under local anasthesia"},{"label":"B","text":"An excisional biopsy under local anesthesia"},{"label":"C","text":"An excision under general anesthesia with permission to do a mastectomy"},{"label":"D","text":"Mammograpy"},{"label":"E","text":"A trial of estrogen therapy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Neoplasia","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2f2120f95679","stem":"An oophorectomy is indicated in the management of a 