ion of the lymphnode follicule - follicules with centroblasts, -centrocytes, -macrophages, -dendritic follicular cells -mantle zone -some T lymphocytes","type":"Short Answer","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3ec01c55c142","stem":"Describe the granuloma of tuberculosis - central area of caseous necrosis - around the necrosis palissading epithelioid cells - some Langhans giant cells - surrounded by a crown of small lymphocytes - coalescence of granulomas","type":"Short Answer","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Infectious Diseases","topicOriginal":"Infectious Diseases","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Infectious Diseases","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-829503f8bec1","stem":"Causes of raised white cell counts include all of the following except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Myelocytic leukaemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Staphylococcal septicaemia"},{"label":"C","text":"HIV disease"},{"label":"D","text":"Acute hemorrhage"},{"label":"E","text":"Lead posoning f) Diabetic ketoacidosis SECTION II - SHORT ESSAY QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft"