rding efficacy and potency of a drug, all are true except: (AI 2002)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"In a clinical setup, efficacy is more important than potency"},{"label":"B","text":"In the log dose response curve, the height of the curve corresponds with efficacy"},{"label":"C","text":"ED50 of the drug corresponds to the efficacy"},{"label":"D","text":"Drugs that produce a similar pharmacological effect can have different levels of efficacy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ab89e612f0ee","stem":"True statement regarding inverse agonist is: (AI 2001)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Binds to the receptor and causes intended action"},{"label":"B","text":"Binds to the receptor and causes opposite action"},{"label":"C","text":"Binds to the receptor and causes no action"},{"label":"D","text":"Binds to the receptor and causes submaximal action"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7a3860d939ca","stem":"All are pharmacogenetic conditions except: (AI 2000)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Adenosine deaminase deficiency"},{"label":"B","text":"Malignant hyperthermia"},{"label":"C","text":"Coumarin insensitivity"},{"label":"D","text":"G-6-PD deficiency"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-072fd60bed15","stem":"Which of the following property of the drug will enable it to be used in low concentration? (AIIMS Nov. 2005)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"High affinity"},{"label":"B","text":"High specificity"},{"label":"C","text":"Low specificity"},{"label":"D","text":"High stability"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3e3d6702384d","stem":"All of the following drugs are contraindicated in patients with G-6-PD deficiency, except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cotrimoxazole\b (AIIMS May, 2004)"},{"label":"B","text":"Furazolidone"},{"label":"C","text":"Nalidixic acid"},{"label":"D","text":"Ceftriaxone"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigu