on"},{"label":"B","text":"Placebo is the inert material added to the drug for making tablets"},{"label":"C","text":"Placebos do not produce any effect"},{"label":"D","text":"All patients respond to placebo"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f0c34e86bf00","stem":"Which of the following statements best describes an ‘orphan drug’?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a drug which acts on orphanin receptors"},{"label":"B","text":"It is a very cheap drug"},{"label":"C","text":"It is a drug which has no therapeutic use"},{"label":"D","text":"It is a drug required for treatment or prevention of a rare disease"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-afac42a25411","stem":"With respect to clinical trials of new drugs, which of the following is most correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phase I involves the study of a small number of nor- mal volunteers by highly trained clinical pharmacol- ogists"},{"label":"B","text":"Phase II involves the use of the new drug in a large number of patients (1000-5000) who have the disease to be treated"},{"label":"C","text":"Phase III involves the determination of the drug’s therapeutic index by the cautious induc­tion of toxicity"},{"label":"D","text":"Phase IV involves the detailed study of toxic effects that have been discovered in phase III. https://kat.cr/user/Blink99/ 32 Review of Pharmacology General Pharmacology"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3ca4ed59416e","stem":"In which of the following phases of clinical trials, healthy normal human volunteers participate","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phase-I (MPPG 2003)"},{"label":"B","text":"Phase-II"},{"label":"C","text":"Phase-III"},{"label":"D","text":"Phase-IV"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e0415a13f18c","stem":"There are some undesirable but unavoidable pharma- codynamic effects of a drug, which are known as","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Toxic effects\b (MPPG 2002)"},{"label":"B","text":"Idiosyncrasy"},{"label":"C","text":"Side effects"},{"label":"D","text":"Intolerance"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"